course: dictionary
lesson: 12038
title: Circulate: moving around
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Circulate means to move round and round, or to pass from one person or place to another. Context tells you which meaning fits. «Blood circulates around your body, going out to your arms and legs and coming back to your heart.» Blood is inside you and it goes round and comes back, so circulate means move round and return.
explain: «The head teacher asked us to circulate a letter to all the parents.» Here the letter goes from person to person, so circulate means pass around. Ask yourself: what is moving, and where does it go?
explain: «At the party, Sam tried to circulate and chat with everyone.» People do not stay in one spot at a party. Sam moves around the room and talks to different people. The clue is the word party, and the meaning is move around among people.
fact: Circulate means to move round, or to pass from person to person or place to place.
fact: «Blood circulates» means blood moves round and round your body and comes back to your heart.
fact: «Rumours circulate» means rumours spread from one person to another.
fact: «Circulate around the room» means move about among people and talk to them.
fact: Circulate is a verb: circulate, circulates, circulated, circulating.
exercise: «Blood circulates around the body.» What does circulates mean here? | Gets very hot | Stops and stays in one place | Turns into bones | *Moves round and round and comes back
exercise: «The head teacher circulated a letter to all the parents.» What did she do with the letter? | Read it out loud to one child | Put it in a box | *Passed it on to many people | Tore it up
exercise: «At the party, Sam tried to circulate and talk to everyone.» What does circulate mean here? | Go to sleep | Sit still in one corner | *Move around and talk to many people | Leave the house
test: «Rumours circulate quickly in a small school.» What does circulate mean? | Freeze in winter | *Spread from person to person | Stop completely | Get bigger each day
test: «Air circulates through the room when the window is open.» What does circulate mean? | *Moves round the room and keeps moving | Stays trapped in one corner | Becomes cold and heavy | Turns into water
exam: «Mia was asked to circulate at the party.» What does circulate mean here? | Throw out the rubbish | *Move around and talk to many people | Hide under the table | Lie down and rest
